summary: MLS Enforcing-Mode Boot Validation (COPR-based validation of PR #3380, EXPERIMENTAL)
description: |
    EXPERIMENTAL sibling of tmt/mls-final.fmf (same directory). Validates
    upstream PR #3380
    (https://github.com/fedora-selinux/selinux-policy/pull/3380, "Enable
    cloud-init under MLS", 2 commits: the cloud-init fix + the udev_t
    MLS-boot-hang fix) as the REAL Packit/COPR-built selinux-policy-mls
    RPM package, instead of manually building/loading standalone .te
    modules on top of an unpatched package.

    Enables the Packit-managed COPR repo
    packit/fedora-selinux-selinux-policy-3380 (confirmed via the GitHub
    API against PR #3380 HEAD c3fbc760b9: rpm-build succeeded for
    fedora-44-x86_64, fedora-45-x86_64 and fedora-rawhide-x86_64) before
    installing selinux-policy-mls. Since dnf/dnf5 picks the highest EVR
    across ALL enabled repos (not just the newly-enabled one), and a
    fast-moving compose can already have a newer selinux-policy-mls build
    than Packit's PR snapshot (observed live on Fedora-Rawhide), the
    prepare script pins the exact NVR Packit built for PR #3380 on the
    fedora-44-x86_64 chroot -- so run this plan against --compose
    Fedora-44, not Fedora-Rawhide.

    This covers 6 of the 8 modules the production plan builds locally
    (cloudform + the 5 udev_t fixes now folded into udev.te upstream);
    mlssshpipes and udevptrace are NOT part of PR #3380 (not present
    anywhere in its diff) and are still built/loaded locally here.

    This is a one-off validation test, NOT a replacement for the
    production tmt/mls-final.fmf plan/mechanism. Do not treat a pass here
    as a reason to change mls-final.fmf without a separate, explicit
    decision to do so.

    Requires environment variable PR_NUMBER (the selinux-policy PR number
    whose Packit-managed COPR build, packit/fedora-selinux-selinux-policy-
    ${PR_NUMBER}, should be installed from). Defaults to 3380 below for
    manual/ad-hoc runs; a CI caller (e.g. `testing-farm request`) should
    override it with `-e PR_NUMBER=<n>` / `--tmt-environment PR_NUMBER=<n>`
    for whichever PR is actually under test.

environment:
  PR_NUMBER: "3380"

prepare:
  - name: Install MLS policy from PR #3380's COPR build, build/load the 2 remaining local fixes, switch to MLS and then Enforcing (2 reboots)
    how: shell
    script: $TMT_TREE/tmt/mls-final-copr-prepare.sh

execute:
  how: tmt
  script: $TMT_TREE/tmt/mls-final-copr-execute.sh
